-- ── Deliberate calls registered during implementation ──

-- C18: `incoming` COLUMN-COORDINATE TRANSPOSITION. The P1 catalog keys
-- incoming as [1,0]/[0,1] — written in EDGE column coordinates (src=0, dst=1;
-- the with_base_relations comment says incoming IS edge's reverse-run view,
-- folded into edge's reverse SortOrder at P3). The P2 projection serves
-- incoming with the §6.2-normative tuple (dst, src, type); a literal reading
-- of [1,0] against THAT tuple would make prefix_scan(incoming, Forward,
-- [Id(dst)]) probe the src column — violating equivalence pair 5. CALL: the
-- adapter transposes incoming's declared vectors into its own tuple
-- coordinates (Forward = (dst,src)-major, Reverse = (src,dst)-major); catalog
-- untouched; documented at the transposition site; disappears entirely at
-- P3's fold. Evidence the call is right: pairs 3b/5/5b green on fixtures AND
-- the real base.
claim_of[a](c18_incoming_edge_coordinate_transposition).
ground[a](c18_incoming_edge_coordinate_transposition, p1_decl_written_in_edge_coords_pair5_defines_the_truth).

-- C19: E-STORE-001 FOR DELEGATED BACKEND FAILURES. §7.2 leaves the Result
-- error type unspecified and the doc taxonomy has no code for an I/O/commit
-- failure PROPAGATED from the store layer; mapping such failures onto
-- E-CAP-001/E-CAT-001 would lie about their nature, and panicking would
-- violate I5. CALL: FactStoreError{code:"E-STORE-001"} wraps GraphError from
-- delegated operations ONLY (commit/compact/flush/durability/open); every
-- FactStore-level REJECTION still uses exactly the four pre-registered codes.
claim_of[a](c19_e_store_001_delegated_failures_only).
ground[a](c19_e_store_001_delegated_failures_only, taxonomy_has_no_backend_failure_code_mislabeling_would_lie).

-- C20: C13 REFINED — stats computed at FIRST OBSERVATION, not construction.
-- Construction-time compute would observe the pre-commit empty state for any
-- adapter that receives writes after opening (exactly the fixture pattern) and
-- would charge every open() the full attr projection even if stats are never
-- read. CALL: the base-five live_facts/live_asserts are computed ONCE, lazily,
-- at the first stats() call (OnceLock), from a snapshot taken at that moment;
-- same sentinel (distinct/max_fanout 0, updated_at_tx 0), same «refresh = new
-- adapter» rule, still nothing consumes stats in P2. The pre-registered
-- "construction-time" wording is superseded by this registration.
claim_of[a](c20_stats_first_observation_refines_c13).
ground[a](c20_stats_first_observation_refines_c13, construction_time_would_observe_pre_commit_empty_state).

-- C21: P2 WRITE VOCABULARY IS Str-VALUED attrs. An attr asserted with an Int/
-- Float/BigInt/Term VALUE cannot round-trip through today's metadata blob:
-- the read projection stringifies scalars (matching today's attr dispatch), so
-- a written Int(5) would read back Str("5") — a DIFFERENT fid. Silent lossy
-- coercion is forbidden (I5), so non-Str attr values are rejected E-CAP-001
-- ("record-vocabulary") together with non-base predicates and malformed
-- record shapes. Numeric metadata written by the LEGACY path still projects
-- (stringified) on read — the restriction is write-side only, exactly the
-- asymmetry today's format imposes. P6's converter (typed columns) lifts it.
claim_of[a](c21_write_attrs_str_only_no_lossy_coercion).
ground[a](c21_write_attrs_str_only_no_lossy_coercion, int_would_read_back_as_str_different_fid_silent_loss_forbidden).

-- C22: DIFFERENTIAL FINDING — the §2.3 conflict class SPLITS today's read
-- paths, and the FactStore projection resolves it winner-coherently. First
-- real-base run FAILED at pair 9 with a REAL divergence:
--   assertion `left == right` failed: 9: count of type 'EXTERNAL_FUNCTION'
--     left: 92  right: 53          (left = type probe, right = count_by_type_at)
-- 92 − 53 = 39 = EXACTLY the §2.3-measured duplicate-id conflicts
-- (GLOBAL_DEFINITION winner shadowing EXTERNAL_FUNCTION). Mechanism read from
-- code: find_nodes_at(Some(ty)) / the executor's scan_nodes_by_type filter by
-- type BEFORE newest-wins dedup (a non-matching newer record never enters
-- `seen`, so the shadowed older record leaks); count_by_type_at dedups BEFORE
-- counting (winner types only). Two production read paths disagree on the same
-- snapshot — the doc's «сегодня выбор делает физика» made mechanically visible
-- for the first time by this differential.
-- CALL: the fact relation must be COHERENT — §7.2 defines prefix_scan as a
-- WINDOW of sorted_run, and sorted_run projects newest-wins winners — so the
-- adapter's type probe resolves candidates through the winner point path and
-- drops shadowed records. The differential asserts fact ≡ oracle MINUS
-- individually-verified shadowed rows (winner type ≠ probed type), records the
-- shadowed total (0 on conflict-free fixtures), and pair 9 stays STRICT
-- against count_by_type_at (winner counts on both sides). Pair 7c gets the
-- same accounting against nodes_by_attr. The class is pinned ON A FIXTURE by
-- facts::differential::duplicate_id_conflict_class_is_coherent_and_explained
-- (two commits, one id, two types: window coherence + oracle leak + strict
-- winner counts + explained differential). Real resolution POLICY (author
-- priority / max tick / min fid + conflict/5 facts) remains §10.4 P5 — the P2
-- winner rule is exactly today's storage physics (newest-wins), not a new
-- policy, so equivalence with the engine's point reads is preserved.
claim_of[a](c22_conflict_class_splits_read_paths_winner_coherent_projection).
ground[a](c22_conflict_class_splits_read_paths_winner_coherent_projection, real_base_92_vs_53_equals_39_documented_conflicts_mechanism_read_from_code).

